Reads each port's own xstats names: `TRexClient._connect` (common/trex_client.py:472-475 at the pin) reads the
names of one port (`any_port`) and gives them to every port, on the stated assumption that "all ports on a given
TRex server instance have the same list of xstats". A server whose ports mix physical and virtual functions breaks
it: a virtual function lists fewer counters. `PortXStats._pre_update` (common/stats/trex_port_stats.py:226) then
raises "Length of get_xstats_names: N and get_port_xstats_values: M" for every port whose list differs, and
`_clear_stats_common` (:2959) clears the xstats of every port, so a Reset or Clear of any one port fails (seen
2026-11-06 on a server with two physical and two virtual-function ports: 91 names against 84 values). The patch
reads each port's names at connect (one more request per port) and, when a port's values no longer match its
names, reads that port's names again once before raising, which also covers a list that changes after connect.
Upstream: not reported. Not touched by any other patch.

diff -ruN a/trex/common/stats/trex_port_stats.py b/trex/common/stats/trex_port_stats.py
--- a/trex/common/stats/trex_port_stats.py	2026-11-06 12:29:51.948314805 -0500
+++ b/trex/common/stats/trex_port_stats.py	2026-11-06 12:29:58.070956257 -0500
@@ -208,6 +208,7 @@
         super(PortXStats, self).__init__(RpcCmdData('get_port_xstats_values', {'port_id': port_obj.port_id}, ''))
 
         self.port_id = port_obj.port_id
+        self.port_obj = port_obj
         self.names = []
 
     @staticmethod
@@ -223,6 +224,10 @@
     def _pre_update(self, snapshot):
         values = snapshot['xstats_values']
 
+        # trex-web-gui patch 17: a list that no longer matches the names read at connect is read again, once
+        if len(values) != len(self.names):
+            self.names = self.get_names(self.port_obj)
+
         if len(values) != len(self.names):
             raise TRexError('Length of get_xstats_names: %s and get_port_xstats_values: %s' % (len(self.names), len(values)))
 
diff -ruN a/trex/common/trex_client.py b/trex/common/trex_client.py
--- a/trex/common/trex_client.py	2026-11-06 12:29:51.946541711 -0500
+++ b/trex/common/trex_client.py	2026-11-06 12:29:58.070785745 -0500
@@ -467,10 +467,10 @@
         if not rc:
             return rc
 
-        xstat_names = self.any_port.xstats.get_names(self.any_port)
-        # all ports on a given TRex server instance have the same list of xstats
+        # trex-web-gui patch 17: each port reads its own xstats names; the ports of one server can list
+        # different counters (a virtual function lists fewer than a physical port)
         for port in self.ports.values():
-            port.xstats.set_names(xstat_names)
+            port.xstats.set_names(port.xstats.get_names(port))
 
         # sync the ports
         rc = self._for_each_port('sync')
